 "notes": [
  "Object list from the NOVOS 7 / NOVOS Touch / thanos EVO operating manual, rev A (13.07.2020), section 5 (pages 19-25). The section heading says 'Modbus Register-Specification' but the tables list BACnet objects. Object names are printed in square brackets; the brackets are dropped here.",
  "NOVOS Touch and thanos EVO are functionally identical and differ only in design.",
  "The Value Light and Value Shutter/Blind AVs carry 0-100 % or a button code (110 = no press, 111/112 = short/long up, 113/114 = short/long down, 115/116 = pressed up/down), depending on how the channel is configured in uConfig.",
  "Which sensor AIs are present depends on the variant (temperature, humidity, CO2, VOC). The manual has no access column; R/W here is inferred from the descriptions."
 ],
